{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1564725-the-liminal-road-a-mastigos-legacy-of-travelers-of-synchronicity-fate-space","id":1564725,"title":"The Liminal Road, a Mastigos Legacy of travelers of synchronicity (Fate/Space)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-13T11:36:55-07:00","id":1564725,"title":"The Liminal Road, a Mastigos Legacy of travelers of synchronicity (Fate/Space)","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Origins</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;The road goes ever on and on, down from the door where it began.&quot;<br /> -J.R.R. Tolkien</i><br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Trekkers<br /> <b>Parentage: </b>Mastigos, Free Council, Mysterium<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> The trekkers do not trace their origin to a single founder. Instead, the Road blossomed independently across the centuries, discovered by mages who shared a singular, profound despair\u2014those feeling utterly paralyzed by a choice, mourning a lost future, or wandering aimlessly through their own lives.<br /> <br /> While traveling a mundane path\u2014a winding forest trail, a fog-rolled Roman highway, or a quiet, modern subway transfer\u2014these mages stepped down an unfamiliar turn. The background noise of the world faded into a soft, ringing hum. A gentle wind stirred, and they found themselves in a forgotten clearing. The canopy above them shifted, and they were bathed in sunlight filtering through leaves in a way that made the dust motes look like frozen stars.<br /> <br /> Wandering through the quiet, each traveler stumbled upon a landmark completely at odds with their era. The journal of an ancient Roman mage recounts passing a strangely smooth shelter of glass and steel. Modern Awakened report finding a moss-covered stone torii gate or an archaic wooden signpost. Yet regardless of the century, one constant remains: resting upon a bench or stone is a traveler\u2019s pack, holding a personal item belonging intimately to that specific mage\u2014but a version they have not yet acquired, or one weathered by decades of future travel.<br /> <br /> It is in taking a breath to appreciate the item, viewing it amidst their surroundings through the lens of Focused Fate Sight, that they discover the Road and can choose to finally step onto it. When they emerge, they arrive at their destination hours or days later, having taken a detour that geographically should not exist.<br /> <br /> The nature of the Clearing has puzzled many Awakened over the ages. Some theorize that it is a wandering Verge, a piece of Arcadia walking the Road to meet travelers. Some believe it is a part of the Hedge, an ever shifting Trod whose gate constantly moves location. Whatever the truth, those trekkers who have passed by it see it as a memorable waypoint on their journey.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearances:</b> A trekker dresses for the journey, prioritizing utility, weather resistance, and comfort without looking totally divorced from local fashion, favoring a gorpcore or high-end street-nomad aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Earthy tones are common, such as forest greens, dark browns and slate greys, which are usually accented by sudden flashes of high-visibility colors, such as a neon trail-marker ribbon tied to a belt, or a bright copper zipper. Heavy duster coats, weather-worn leather jackets, oilskin parkas, or rugged trench coats with plenty of deep, hidden pockets are also favored. High-quality, perfectly broken-in hiking boots, sturdy leather riding boots, or tactical sneakers are staples amongst them. A trekker's shoes are always clean and well-maintained, no matter how dirty the rest of their gear is.<br /> <br /> In order to carry their gear, trekkers usually have a heavy-duty canvas rucksack or a high-tech internal-frame backpack, normally expanded via Space magic to hold more than it should. They are usually packed full of supplies and navigation tools of all types, such as vintage brass compasses and hand-drawn maps on parchment overlapping printed satellite imagery. Some of them even contain Irises to a Sanctum.<br /> <br /> Reflecting their affinity for travel, their Sanctums are often found in places of transition, such as an abandoned subway station, a converted shipping container in a bustling shipyard, a forgotten cabin at a highway dead-end, or the back room of a 24-hour diner. The walls are typically plastered with maps, train and bus schedules, and strings connecting physical photographs. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Doctrine</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;Do not go where the path may lead, go instead where there is no path and leave a trail.&quot;<br /> -Ralph Waldo Emerson</i><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Fate 2, Survival 2<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b> The prospective member makes their way to a location they are not familiar with, traditionally chosen through a mentor's own Attainments. From there, they must then &quot;follow the white rabbit down the rabbithole&quot;, utilizing Fate magic to guide them to discover a token of what they need but do not yet know. It is the act of intuitively finding waypoints amidst an unfamiliar topography\u2014alongside experiencing a moment of self-discovery when they appreciate the item with Focused Fate Sight\u2014that completes their initiation into the Road.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> The trekkers see themselves as a vast constellation of travelers whose paths sometimes cross. Because of this, they have no central governing body, no single leader, and no permanent headquarters. In their place they have the Crossroads Network, a series of Waystations that trekkers organically gather around\u2014specific places such as Sanctums, 24-hour highway diners, or abandoned train platforms. They use coded trail markers, created with Fate and Space, to mark which Waystations are active.<br /> <br /> At every major Waystation, there is a hidden journal or digital ledger. Trekkers use it to log dangerous anomalies or safe shortcuts through the city. They don't command each other; they simply leave a map for whoever comes next. If a trekker needs help, they don't order another member to assist. They ask to &quot;walk together for a mile.&quot; If another trekker agrees, their paths join until the problem is solved, after which they part ways with zero expectations or debts.<br /> <br /> Master and apprentice often share a close bond. The mentor knows it is not their role to mark a trail for their apprentice, but to guide them as they stumble, make mistakes and find a path on their own.<br /> <br /> When a time comes that their Roads separate, they share a final meal or a drink at a crossroads, swap a token (like a trail marker or a ticket stub), and walk in completely opposite directions. No matter how long it takes for their paths to cross again, the trekkers rarely view this with sadness, finding great comfort in knowing a friend still graces the world with their skills, their viewpoint and their present.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory:</b> Life is a continuous journey, countless roads branch off from each moment. Some of them obvious, others so subtle that we might not even know they exist. Each one leads us through numerous waypoints towards a myriad possible destinations.<br /> <br /> Just like we can teach our minds to navigate our environment, so too can we train our intuition to guide us through the trails of possibility. It is only when we learn to find our way in both the natural and supernatural landscape as one that we can make our path through the world.<br /> <br /> Journey through the roads of synchronicity, learn the secret topography of existence and find the way towards the future you envision. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Magic</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>\u201cLearn to trust the journey, even when you do not understand it.&quot;<br /> -Lolly Daskal</i><br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Fate<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Navigation tools (+1), train stations, airports, bus stops or other travel nodes (+1, +2 for supernatural ones), crossroads (+1), liminal spaces (+1), trail markers (+1), tickets, passports, toll receipt or other symbols of permitted travel (+1), making a Survival roll related to the spell (+2).<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Traveling, finding and exploring a secret passage or hidden path, buying or acquiring a souvenir, writing a record of one's travels (letter, journal, blog, etc), making or updating a map, sharing knowledge of paths and roads with others, swapping travel stories or road advice with a stranger, marking a trail.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">First: Wanderer's Grace</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiation<br /> <br /> The trekkers believe there are no wrong turnings, only paths they did not know they were meant to walk. Their steps naturally follow the paths of synchronicity, leading them towards auspicious encounters.<br /> <br /> This replicates <i>Reading the Outmost Eddies</i> with Reach assigned to instant use and advanced duration. However, it may only be used on the trekker themselves. With conjuctional Space 1, they can nudge fortuitous strands of fate closer, receiving results within an hour.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: </b>Space 1<br /> <br /> A trekker understands being ready for the Road is how one ensures smooth travels. After a scene preparing for a journey (securing supplies, gear or maps; calibrating equipment, etc), or guiding a subject through the process, events conspire to pave the trail they blaze.<br /> <br /> This replicates <i>Green Light, Red Light</i> as a Compelling of Fate and Space, with Reach assigned to advanced duration. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Second:</b> Journeyer\u2019s Intuition</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Fate 2, Direction Sense<br /> <br /> When faced with the riddles of the road, a trekker's instincts point them in the right direction. They choose the right path at the crossroads, guess the password to a computer, discover the number of the ally they need to talk to, and more.<br /> <br /> This replicates <i>Lucky Number</i> with Reach assigned to instant use.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Space 2<br /> <br /> The trekker knows the true value of a journey lies in the experiences one has along the way. After a scene exploring a location, or doing so alongside a subject, they develop an innate ability to appreciate the landscape of synchronicity.<br /> <br /> This replicates <i>Interconnections </i>with Reach assigned to advanced duration and detecting supernatural changes to fate. With conjunctional Space 2, they can delve into the details about the fates of those they observe. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Third: </b>Desire\u2019s Path</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Fate 3, Survival 3<br /> <br /> The trekker spontaneously reads the synchronicitous signs around them, orienteering the next steps on their journey.<br /> <br /> This replicates <i>Serendipity </i>with Reach assigned to instant use, advanced duration and substituting for another skill in the same category. Should they also possess conjunctional Space 2, they are able to find the most appropriate road, allowing any skill to be substituted.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Space 3<br /> <br /> When the trekker finds their path blocked, they trust their gut to reveal the way forward, allowing them to continue their journey.<br /> <br /> This replicates <i>Break Boundary</i> with Reach assigned to instant use and passing through narrow paths. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Fourth:</b> Seeker\u2019s Stride</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Fate 4, Survival 4<br /> <br /> A trekker walks the Road confident that each step taken is one step closer to their next milestone. They set out into the world, holding a goal in mind, following the pull of intuition from one synchronicitous waypoint to another. After following this path for a scene, they come upon a sign related to their goal, indicating they stepped on the road to realize it. They may also do this for others, by guiding them through the process.<br /> <br /> This replicates <i>Strings of Fate</i> with Reach assigned to advanced duration. Should they also have conjunctional Space 3, they can choose the perfect thread to follow, allowing them to find opportunities once a day.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: </b>Space 4<br /> <br /> The trekker is instinctively aware of the occult landscape around them and knows every shortcut, being able to step from one point to another in moments.<br /> <br /> This replicates <i>Teleportation</i> with Reach assigned to instant use.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Fifth: </b>Wayfinder\u2019s Horizon</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Fate 5, Survival 5<br /> <br /> The greatest trekkers don't just ride into the horizon, they chart the journey ahead. After spending a scene writing a bucket list of the milestones they wish to experience on their journey, or doing so for someone else, fate conspires to bring them to fruition.<br /> <br /> This replicates <i>Forge Destiny</i> with Reach assigned to advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Space 5<br /> <br /> A souvenir carries a map of a journey within it, and for those that can read it, it can be used to mark a trail. After a scene tracing the paths of synchronicity and sympathy on an item, the trekker is able to create a permanent trail towards a waypoint.<br /> <br /> This replicates <i>Co-Location</i>, with Reach assigned to sympathetic range, indefinite duration and advanced scale. A single point of mana pays for Sympathetic Range, Everywhere and indefinite duration. With conjunctional Fate 2, a Key can be applied to it as well.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">What were you thinking design wise ?</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The first Attainment allows them to feel the flow of synchronicity, giving them opportunities and positive twists of fate regularly. Since it's not the most powerful spell, but it is thematic, the restriction of only being able to use it on themselves makes up for it. With conjunctional Space 1, they can locate those positive points on the Road more easily, allowing them to get results faster.<br /> <br /> The first optional Attainment lets them locate auspicious threads of probability and nudge them closer, ensuring they always make good time on their travels or are at the right place and at the right time.<br /> <br /> The second main Attainment makes it so when there is uncertainty on their path, they can always intuitively find the way forward. The right way to follow at a crossroads, the password for the computer, the number of the ally they need to talk to, etc.<br /> <br /> The second optional Attainment allows them to delve into and understand the nuances of fate, gaining understanding about the Road they and those around them walk. With conjunctional Space 2, they can see how it all fits together in much richer details.<br /> <br /> The third main Attainment makes it so they can always sense the path with an opportunity that plays to their strengths. With conjunctional Space 2, they can find the exact thread of possibility they are looking for.<br /> <br /> The third optional Attainment makes it so that few obstacles can bar their path. If there is even the tiniest gap for passage, they can overcome it.<br /> <br /> The fourth main Attainment allows them to follow the trail of synchronicity to find their goal. With conjunctional Space 3, they can locate the perfect thread to follow to travel to their goal faster.<br /> <br /> The fourth optional Attainment makes it so everywhere that is within sensory range becomes instantly reachable, allowing them to cross vast distances in moments.<br /> <br /> The capstone makes it so they don't just follow the Road, they define it through their commitment to their bucket list. It can grant a Destiny without a Doom, bestow supernatural merits, even change Aspirations and Obsession, allowing the trekker to adapt to and grow with the journey more easily.<br /> <br /> The optional capstone allows them to create their own private travel network around the world, allowing them to cross vast distances within moments. It's not as important to understand where the journey of life will take you next, but to appreciate the experiences along the way and grow with them.<br /> <br /> The core design phrase of the Legacy was &quot;making a path through the world&quot;, and the feeling I was trying to capture was that of komorebi.<br /> <br /> The background provided a moment of komorebi when someone has reached a &quot;dead end&quot; on their road, allowing them to find a new path once they take a moment to appreciate the experience and find what they need. The initiation echoes this idea.<br /> <br /> The appearances show they are always ready to travel, having both appropriate clothes, gear and supplies for the journey. It also shows that they leverage Space magic to ensure they always have what they need on hand. The location of their Sanctums makes it easy for them to embark on the Road and the maps reflect their holistic approach to traveling the material and metaphysical.<br /> <br /> Since trekkers are usually on the Road, I imagined they would favor a decentralized structure, founded on solidarity of helping others along their Road. The practice of leaving aid behind is inspired by geocaching.<br /> <br /> The master and student relationship is inspired by Grand Admiral Thrawn's quote of friendship, making it a close bond, but a very unpossessive one. The teaching method is inspired by Oogway from <i>Kung Fu Panda</i>, whose approach to mentorship guides and fosters growth, but without ownership of what form that growth will take.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the yantras and oblations are meant to put them in places where they will have interesting encounters, to seek out liminal spaces and to take souvenirs to help them remember the experiences they had on their Road.<br /> <br /> That concludes the design notes, hope you had as much fun reading them as I had writing them.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}